From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] memory: every allocation pool access is locked, and running out of memory no longer dereferences null

importImageResource and the sparse createAllocation popped the allocation pool
without the allocator's lock while DXVK's cs and submit threads allocated and
freed under it, and the embedder imports host images on its own threads, so
the pool's free list was corrupted and the next allocation crashed.
When no memory is left, allocateStorage returns null: the DxvkBuffer and
DxvkImage constructors throw DxvkOutOfMemoryError, which the Direct3D 11
Create calls return as E_OUTOFMEMORY and Map(WRITE_DISCARD) returns as such
before touching the slice. On the cs thread nothing throws: invalidateBuffer,
storage relocation and the temporary, zero, spec data and scratch buffers
skip the operation and mark the device lost.
---
diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.h b/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.h
index 52309c35..3d69a225 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.h
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_buffer.h
@@ -125,7 +125,10 @@ namespace dxvk {
     
     Rc<DxvkResourceAllocation> DiscardSlice(DxvkLocalAllocationCache* cache) {
       auto allocation = m_buffer->allocateStorage(cache);
-      m_mapPtr = allocation->mapPtr();
+
+      if (likely(allocation))
+        m_mapPtr = allocation->mapPtr();
+
       return allocation;
     }
 
